      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "The apartment has vanished. No more tiled floors, no more Tori Amos posters on the walls, no more anything. Instead, the",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1082
        }
      ],
      "words": 24
    },
    {
      "block": "原句2",
      "no": 2,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "This is a hallucination. On the right there’s an island of luxurious vegetation",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1637
        }
      ],
      "words": 13
    },
    {
      "block": "原句3",
      "no": 3,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "In this urban condo, as far from the sea as from every illusion of magic, the young woman has drowned",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 4782
        }
      ],
      "words": 20
    },
    {
      "block": "原句4",
      "no": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "A glint of recognition flashes through his eyes, so rapid that a less attentive observer wouldn’t have seen it",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 5688
        }
      ],
      "words": 19
    },
    {
      "block": "原句5",
      "no": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Home is a safe place, your place above all, so much yours as to be part of you. If someone enters it, explores it withou",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 11271
        }
      ],
      "words": 47
    },
    {
      "block": "原句6",
      "no": 6,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "It’s a moment of epiphany: nothing is clear, and yet in a sense everything is, because it has to be. Wendy will have to ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 13199
        }
      ],
      "words": 35
    },
    {
      "block": "原句7",
      "no": 7,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“Adamaria’s drowned,” he finishes. “Her clothes were soaked. Believe me, it wasn’t a hallucination.”",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 13549
        }
      ],
      "words": 14
    },
    {
      "block": "原句8",
      "no": 8,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "She thought she was brave. She thought she was strong. But she’s never been hit, never been beaten",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 15279
        }
      ],
      "words": 18
    },
    {
      "block": "原句9",
      "no": 9,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "“I’m killing you,” says Captain Hook",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 16668
        }
      ],
      "words": 6
    },
    {
      "block": "原句10",
      "no": 10,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "A beach and a verdant forest appear, and it isn’t raining like in Rome, there’s tropical sunlight",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 17198
        }
      ],
      "words": 17
    },
    {
      "block": "原句11",
      "no": 11,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Heroes stand firm against villains. Why should I",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 19119
        }
      ],
      "words": 8
    },
    {
      "block": "原句12",
      "no": 12,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Your god will not return to earth, not now or ever",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 22165
        }
      ],
      "words": 11
    },
    {
      "block": "原句13",
      "no": 13,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "You healed the mad, Stefano: your mistake was joining them",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 22700
        }
      ],
      "words": 10
    },
    {
      "block": "原句14",
      "no": 14,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Michele is the only one who can communicate with them all: a shaman, now, he lives halfway between worlds",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 38162
        }
      ],
      "words": 19
    },
    {
      "block": "原句15",
      "no": 15,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "And that’s how the boy becomes a man, learning what cruelty is, learning what hatred is, with nobody left to protect him",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 41106
        }
      ],
      "words": 25
    }
